Thank you. Below is a complete CAPA framework you can use right away. Since the Problem Description is not provided, I’ve included a fully editable CAPA Report template with placeholders. I’ve also included a concise, high-level plan aligned to your 10-step approach, and a ready-to-fill Timeline, Responsibilities, and Verification Plan.
High-level approach (concise, not internal reasoning)
•	Step 1: Understand the problem and scope clearly (what, where, when, impact).
•	Step 2: Contain the issue to prevent recurrence in the short term (immediate actions).
•	Step 3: Perform root cause analysis using 5 Whys and validate the root cause(s).
•	Step 4: Determine and validate corrective actions that fix the root cause(s).
•	Step 5: Determine preventive actions to prevent recurrence in the process/system.
•	Step 6: Assign owners and due dates for all actions.
•	Step 7: Define a verification plan to confirm effectiveness.
•	Step 8: Execute actions, collect evidence, and document results.
•	Step 9: Review effectiveness and close CAPA when criteria are met.
•	Step 10: Create formal CAPA report, timeline, responsibilities, and verification plan.
