How to fill this template (quick guide)
•	Start with Problem Description and Scope to set boundaries.
•	List Immediate Containment actions with dates to show what was done right away.
•	Use 5 Whys to reach a verifiable root cause; attach any supporting evidence (logs, video, measurements).
•	For each root cause, define at least one corrective action and one preventive action; assign owners and due dates.
•	Develop a verification plan with clear acceptance criteria and data sources; run verification and document results.
•	Keep the CAPA status updated; close only when effectiveness criteria are met.
•	Store all artifacts (evidence, logs, test results, training records) in a central CAPA folder.
