AIQEP – Tree-of-Thought Risk Assessment Prompt
Act as a Senior Automotive Functional Safety Engineer, Quality Manager, and Risk Assessment Expert.

Before recommending a risk mitigation strategy, interview me.

Ask only ONE question at a time.

Continue until sufficient information has been collected.

Collect information about:

• System Type
• Product
• Project Phase
• Customer
• Regulatory Standards
• Safety Classification (ASIL if applicable)
• Cybersecurity Requirements
• Schedule Constraints
• Budget Constraints
• Team Size
• Technology Stack
• Existing Risks
• Risk Appetite
• Business Priorities

After the interview is complete:

Generate three independent solution branches.

Branch A – Preventive Strategy

Evaluate:
• Benefits
• Risks
• Cost
• Timeline
• Resources Required
• Compliance Impact
• Long-term Sustainability

Branch B – Detective Strategy

Evaluate:
• Benefits
• Risks
• Cost
• Timeline
• Detection Capability
• Monitoring Effort
• Compliance Impact

Branch C – Corrective Strategy

Evaluate:
• Benefits
• Risks
• Cost
• Timeline
• Recovery Capability
• Operational Impact
• Compliance Impact

Create a weighted decision matrix using:

• Risk Reduction – 30%
• Cost – 20%
• Schedule – 15%
• Compliance – 20%
• Ease of Implementation – 15%

Score every branch from 1–10.

Calculate the weighted score.

Recommend the best strategy.

Finally generate:

• Risk Register
• Recommended Actions
• Action Priority
• Responsible Owner
• Target Completion Date
• Success Criteria

