Example CAPA Generator
Question 1: Please provide a concise problem statement including: The exact nonconformity or failure mode The affected product/system (model, part numbers, and revision if applicable) The initial customer impact and symptoms Any known geographic or production batch/vin ranges Any containment actions that have already been taken (Answer this with as much concrete detail as you have available.)
Problem Statement

A critical software defect was identified during System Integration Testing in the Body Control Module (BCM). The ECU intermittently fails to control the automatic headlamp function after multiple ignition ON/OFF cycles. The issue occurs due to incorrect software state transition handling, resulting in loss of the automatic lighting feature.

Affected Product/System

Product: Body Control Module (BCM)
ECU Software Version: BCM_SW_v3.2.1
Hardware Revision: Rev C
Platform: Automotive ECU
Project: Next Generation Passenger Vehicle Program

Initial Customer Impact and Symptoms

Automatic headlamps do not switch ON under low-light conditions.
Driver intervention is required.
Potential customer dissatisfaction and increased warranty claims.
Safety concern due to reduced visibility during night driving.

Geographic / Production Batch

Prototype vehicles used for System Integration Testing.
Approximately 20 evaluation vehicles affected.
No customer production vehicles released.
Production SOP planned for July 2027.

Containment Actions Already Taken

Release of affected software build stopped immediately.
Defect logged in Jira (Defect ID: BCM-4587).
Root cause investigation initiated by Software Development and Quality teams.
Regression testing suspended until corrective software patch is available.
Project stakeholders and Functional Safety Manager notified.
Daily defect review meetings initiated until closure.

Question 2: Please provide the current risk assessment for this BCM software failure, including: Severity, Occurrence, and Detection ratings (as used in your PFMEA or risk matrix) and the resulting RPN Any PFMEA reference(s) or risk-register entries related to the BCM automatic headlamp control and software state transitions Any interim risk mitigations or safety controls you’ve implemented (even ifTemporary) Any data or criteria you’re using to justify the current risk levels (e.g., test results, logs, failure modes)

Current Risk Assessment

Severity (S): 8/10

Failure of the automatic headlamp function can reduce driver visibility during low-light conditions.
Although manual headlamp operation is available, delayed activation presents a potential safety concern and affects customer confidence.

Occurrence (O): 4/10

The issue is intermittent and has been reproduced in approximately 3 out of 20 prototype vehicles during System Integration Testing.
It occurs after repeated ignition ON/OFF cycles under specific software state transition conditions.

Detection (D): 5/10

The defect is detectable during System Integration Testing using automated test cases and manual verification.
Existing Unit Testing did not identify the issue because the software state transition sequence was not fully covered.
