It creates a rich foundation for the next CAPA interview questions on root cause analysis, corrective actions, preventive actions, and effectiveness verification.

Question 3: What is the proposed scope and plan for the corrective action (PCA) and release strategy? Please specify: Whether the fix will be software-only (e.g., BCM_SW_v3.2.2 or later) or if hardware changes are required. A high-level verification plan (unit tests, integration tests, system/vehicle tests) and the acceptance criteria to close the CAPA. Any preliminary owners or leads for the PCA and verification activities.
Proposed Corrective Action (PCA) Scope

The corrective action will be a software-only fix. No hardware changes are currently required, as the investigation indicates the issue is caused by incorrect software state transition logic within the Body Control Module (BCM).

Software Release

Current Version: BCM_SW_v3.2.1
Corrective Release: BCM_SW_v3.2.2
Hardware Revision: Rev C (No Change)
Software Change Request: SCR-BCM-127
Change Classification: Major Software Defect Fix

The software update will:

Correct the state transition logic for the automatic headlamp control.
Improve error handling during repeated ignition ON/OFF cycles.
Add diagnostic logging for unexpected state transitions.
Update software documentation and traceability records.
High-Level Verification Plan
1. Unit Testing

Objective:
Verify the corrected software logic at module level.

Activities:

State transition logic validation.
Boundary condition testing.
Code review.
Static analysis.
Unit test execution.

Acceptance Criteria:

100% of modified functions pass.
No Critical or High severity defects.
Static analysis findings resolved.
2. Integration Testing

Objective:
Verify interaction between BCM software modules.

Activities:

CAN communication validation.
LIN communication validation.
State machine transition verification.
Ignition ON/OFF cycle testing.
Regression testing.

Acceptance Criteria:

No unexpected state transitions.
Automatic headlamp activation functions correctly.
No regression defects introduced.
3. System / Vehicle Testing

Objective:
Validate the complete feature in vehicle conditions.

Activities:

Functional verification.
Low-light automatic headlamp testing.
Repeated ignition cycle testing.
Environmental testing.
End-to-End vehicle validation.

Acceptance Criteria:

Automatic headlamp activates correctly under all specified operating conditions.
Zero reproducible failures after 500 consecutive ignition cycles.
All customer requirements successfully verified.
Functional Safety requirements remain satisfied.
Customer acceptance tests successfully completed.
